# posts resource

This resource was generated by `admin:make-resource`.

## Generated files

- `manifest.go`: Resource metadata and fields.
- `model.go`: ORM model skeleton.
- `request.go`: request boundary.
- `repository.go`: persistence boundary.
- `service.go`: business-service boundary.
- `controller.go`: HTTP boundary.
- `routes.go`: route boundary.
- `permissions.go`: permission boundary.
- `manifest_test.go`: generated manifest test.
- `backend/database/migrations/*_create_posts_table.go`: migration proposal.
- `app/modules/posts/permissions/`: generated permission constants.
- `app/modules/posts/menu/`: generated menu metadata.
- `admin/src/modules/posts/`: frontend metadata, routes and page skeletons.
- `admin/src/modules/posts/api.ts`: list/show/create/update/delete API contract.

## Automatic activation

1. Review the generated files and implement the business behavior.
2. The generator updates the generated backend Registry and frontend discovery files automatically.
3. Review the generated form fields, shared page behavior, and authorization metadata.
4. Review the migration file and execute it manually only after approval.
5. Add the generated migration type to `backend/bootstrap/migrations.go`, then run `go run . artisan migrate`.
6. Assign the generated permissions to an appropriate role from the RBAC page or API.

For an `own` resource, generate an integer owner field with `--owner-field` and use `--scope=own`. Role assignments can then select the Own data only option; the backend sets the owner from the authenticated user and ignores client-supplied owner IDs.

The generator does not modify manually maintained runtime files and does not execute migrations.

## Verification

From `backend/` run:

```text
go test ./...
```
